# linear-tui stores its OAuth token next to its config. Only config.json and
# prompts.json are tracked (see push.sh); this is a second line of defence so
# the token can never be committed by a stray `git add .`.
linear/credentials.json
linear/*.log
linear/*.bak

# Generic secret shapes, in case another tool's config lands here.
*credentials.json
*.pem
*.key

# Backups left by link.sh when it adopts a file an application rewrote, and by
# pull.sh when it displaces a live file. Both are recovery copies, not config.
*.bak
*_bak

# Claude Code syncs first-party skills (pdf, docx, xlsx, pptx, ...) into
# ~/.claude/skills/synced/, which link.sh points at claude/skills/, so they land
# in the working tree. They are Anthropic's, re-downloaded on any machine that
# signs in, and 4 MB of them. Never commit them; this repo is public.
claude/skills/synced/
